==============================================================================
PART 1: safe CONTINUITY along a lift ray (equicontinuity of safe)
==============================================================================
  2-torus U (base AP, lift {4,6}): safe_2d(2/25) = 0.02720
  safe_1d(w^N) for w^N = a + N*b, growing N (should -> safe_2d):
    N=  13: safe_1d = 0.00000  (|safe_1d - safe_2d| = 0.02720)
    N=  25: safe_1d = 0.03347  (|safe_1d - safe_2d| = 0.00627)
    N=  50: safe_1d = 0.03327  (|safe_1d - safe_2d| = 0.00607)
    N= 100: safe_1d = 0.03170  (|safe_1d - safe_2d| = 0.00450)
    N= 200: safe_1d = 0.03007  (|safe_1d - safe_2d| = 0.00287)
    N= 400: safe_1d = 0.02990  (|safe_1d - safe_2d| = 0.00270)
  => convergence safe_1d -> safe_2d confirms safe is CONTINUOUS along
     the lift ray (Weyl equidistribution) -- the equicontinuity of safe.

